WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.862
Now SailPoint and Graph.

2
00:00:01.862 --> 00:00:07.588
The drift and re-read clients need read
scopes only: search read, and accounts read.

3
00:00:07.588 --> 00:00:10.990
The Accounts endpoints would
accept the manage scope too,

4
00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:15.526
so the call list names the read scope
and the comparison flags manage as extra.

5
00:00:15.526 --> 00:00:19.434
Creating SailPoint's workflows
needs the workflow manage scope,

6
00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:21.750
and no client in the kit makes that call.

7
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.359
So, as design guidance, that scope
belongs to a separate client,

8
00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:30.787
used once, by hand or by a reviewed
pipeline, and then removed.

9
00:00:30.787 --> 00:00:35.573
On Graph, the app registration needs
User dot Read dot All, as an application

10
00:00:35.573 --> 00:00:40.126
permission, and AuditLog dot Read dot
All only if the run reads the audit.

11
00:00:40.126 --> 00:00:45.960
Nothing in Pass 1 needs write access to
Entra ID, Active Directory or SailPoint.
